course: dictionary
lesson: 4063
title: Gentle: kind, soft, or not steep
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gentle has more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one. «Be gentle with the puppy; hold it softly.» Here gentle means kind and careful, not rough.
explain: Gentle can also describe something soft or light, like «a gentle breeze», or a slope that rises slowly, not steeply. A gentle sound is quiet and calm.
explain: Ask yourself what the word describes. A person, an animal or a giant? Then gentle is about kindness. A breeze, a slope or a sound? Then gentle means soft, light or not strong. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Gentle means kind and careful, not rough or violent.
fact: Gentle means soft or light, not strong, as in «a gentle breeze».
fact: A gentle slope is not steep: it rises slowly.
fact: «A real Great Dane is huge but gentle and calm.» A gentle giant is big but kind.
fact: Gentle is an adjective. Its forms are gentler and gentlest.
exercise: «Be gentle with the puppy; hold it softly and speak quietly.» What does gentle mean here? | *Kind and careful, not rough | Wet and cold | Strong and fierce | Very loud and fast
exercise: «A gentle breeze moved the leaves.» What does gentle mean here? | Tall and thin | Very hot | *Soft and light, not strong | Dangerous and stormy
exercise: «The path had a gentle slope, so the cart was easy to push up.» What does gentle describe? | A loud noise | A sharp, sudden drop | A kind giant | *A slope that is not steep
test: «The gentle giant helped the children carry the heavy box.» What does gentle giant mean? | Lost in the forest | Very small and shy | Angry and loud | *Big but kind
test: «Her gentle voice calmed the frightened baby.» What does gentle mean here? | Loud and angry | Cold and rough | *Quiet and calm | Fast and excited
exam: Ravi says gentle means weak. What is the best reply? | *Not quite: gentle can mean kind and careful, and a gentle slope is just not steep | Gentle means very fast | Yes, gentle always means weak | Gentle means cold
